WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.018
Federal Contract Information and Controlled Unclassified Information are central to CMMC because

00:00:05.018 --> 00:00:09.936
the type of information in an environment helps determine the required protection

00:00:09.936 --> 00:00:11.576
level and assessment scope.

00:00:11.576 --> 00:00:16.494
FCI is generally nonpublic information provided by or generated for the government

00:00:16.494 --> 00:00:21.002
under a contract to develop or deliver a product or service.

00:00:21.002 --> 00:00:26.330
Publicly available information and simple transactional payment information are excluded from that concept.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.248
CUI is unclassified information that requires safeguarding or dissemination controls under law,

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:32.887
regulation, or government-wide policy.

00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:38.215
The CUI Registry and contract documentation help identify applicable categories and handling expectations.

00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:42.314
CUI is not the same as classified national security information.

00:00:42.314 --> 00:00:48.051
Even though it is unclassified, its loss or unauthorized disclosure can still harm missions,

00:00:48.051 --> 00:00:50.920
individuals, programs, business relationships, or national interests.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.970
Information identification must be deliberate.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:58.297
Teams need to understand what information the contract provides, what their work generates,

00:00:58.297 --> 00:01:01.986
which markings or clauses apply, where the information moves,

00:01:01.986 --> 00:01:05.265
and which systems or people interact with it.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:10.183
Data flow matters because protected information may appear in email, collaboration platforms,

00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:14.281
engineering tools, ticketing systems, source repositories, backups, exports, portable media,

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:16.330
support records, and third-party services.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:20.019
Scope can often be improved by reducing unnecessary movement.

00:01:20.019 --> 00:01:24.527
Organizations may separate covered work, limit approved tools, clarify storage locations,

00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:31.085
and avoid placing FCI or CUI in systems that were not designed or governed for it.

00:01:31.085 --> 00:01:33.134
When information status is unclear,

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:37.642
employees should follow organizational procedures and seek guidance from contract, security,

00:01:37.642 --> 00:01:39.282
legal, or information-governance personnel.

00:01:39.282 --> 00:01:43.380
Guessing can create both protection gaps and unnecessary operational burden.
